.TH OFFLINE 1 "2026-09" "offline" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
offline \- run a program with its network access fully isolated
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B offline
.RB [ \-\-keep\-loopback ]
.RB [ \-\-log\-external ]
.I program
.RI [ args ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B offline
runs
.I program
with its network access fully isolated: private user, network, mount, IPC and
UTS namespaces, an emptied capability set, and a seccomp filter refusing the
network syscalls.
.PP
The program's exit status is mirrored back, so
.B offline
is transparent to a script that wraps it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-loopback
Keep the loopback interface (127.0.0.1) up and reachable. Useful for a test
suite that talks to a server it started itself.
.TP
.B \-\-log\-external
Log blocked network syscalls to standard error, rather than failing them
silently.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status of
.IR program .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run a test suite with no network at all:
.PP
.RS
.B offline pytest \-q
.RE
.PP
Allow a locally started server, and report what was blocked:
.PP
.RS
.B offline \-\-keep\-loopback \-\-log\-external npm test
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unshare (1),
.BR seccomp (2).
Project documentation:
.UR https://github.com/fabiocicerchia/offline
.UE
